.TH CMUX 1 "" "cmux @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cmux \- terminal multiplexer TUI for AI coding agents, backed by libghostty\-vt
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cmux
.RI [ "START OPTIONS" ]
.br
.B cmux attach
.RI [ "START OPTIONS" ]
.RB [ \-\-terminal
.IR terminal-id ]
.br
.B cmux relay
.RI [ "ROUTING OPTIONS" ]
.br
.B cmux machine\-agent
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B cmux
.RI [ "GLOBAL OPTIONS" ]
.I resource action
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cmux
keeps a tree of machines, sessions, workspaces, screens, panes, tabs,
terminals and browsers, and exposes those resources through the
.B cmux.protocol/1
public interface.
.PP
Running
.B cmux
with no resource argument starts or attaches to a session TUI. Every other
invocation is a noun\-first control command that sends one public resource
request to a running session.
.PP
The default session is
.BR main .
Default sockets live at
.IR $TMPDIR/cmux\-tui\-<uid>/<session>.sock .
Detach from an attached TUI with the prefix key followed by
.BR d ,
which is
.B Ctrl\-b d
by default.
.SH PROCESS MODES
.TP
.B cmux
Start a session, or attach to it when it already exists.
.TP
.B cmux attach
Open the complete session TUI. With
.BR \-\-terminal " " \fIterminal-id\fR
it renders only that one PTY terminal, using the full host terminal without
the sidebar, status bar, pane border or other tabs. Startup attach requires an
exact ID from
.BR "cmux terminal list" ;
it does not accept names or
.BR current .
.TP
.B cmux relay
Copy private protocol bytes between standard I/O and one session socket.
Machine connectors use this as a transport primitive; it is not an interactive
TUI.
.TP
.B cmux machine\-agent
Share an existing local session through one outbound SSH registration. Prints a
one\-time pairing code and opens no listener. Unix only.
.SH START OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-session " name"
Select the session name. Defaults to
.BR main .
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " path"
Use an explicit socket path instead of the default location.
.TP
.B \-\-headless
Run the session without attaching a TUI.
.TP
.BI \-\-term " value"
Set
.B TERM
for child PTYs. Without it children get
.BR xterm\-256color .
The
.B CMUX_TUI_TERM
environment variable overrides the terminal runtime default.
.TP
.B \-\-cloud
Compose local machine targets with the Cloud catalog and enable temporary
machine connections without sending local SSH details to Cloud.
.SH SELECTORS
An instance selector accepts a typed opaque ID such as
.IR ws_… ,
.I pane_…
or
.IR term_… ;
the literal
.BR current ;
or an exact name.
.PP
Names may be empty, contain Unicode or whitespace, and need not be unique.
.BI name: value
forces name interpretation and is required for names equal to
.BR current ,
names containing
.BR _ ,
reserved command words, and ID\-shaped names. An ambiguous name returns
.B selector.ambiguous
with every candidate ID; it never chooses one or changes state.
.PP
A direct opaque target ID may omit structural ancestors. A name or
.B current
target requires its complete parent chain.
.SH RESOURCES
The public resource roots are:
.BR machine ", " session ", " client ", " workspace ", " screen ", " pane ,
.BR tab ", " terminal ", " browser ", " notification ", " agent ", " sidebar ,
.BR pairing ", " projection ", " provider " and " raw .
.PP
Run
.BI "cmux " resource " \-\-help"
for the exact paths and flags of one resource.
.SH ROUTING OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-machine " selector"
Routing default for the target machine.
.TP
.BI \-\-session " selector"
Routing default for the target session.
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " path"
Select an exact local socket.
.SH OUTPUT
The output modes are mutually exclusive. With no flag the CLI prints concise
human text on standard output and diagnostics on standard error.
.TP
.B \-\-json
One JSON result or structured error.
.TP
.B \-\-jsonl
One JSON value per result, stream item, or stream end.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
No successful output.
.PP
JSON modes preserve the server's error code, message, details and retryable
flag. Requests are limited to 4 MiB; responses and stream items to 16 MiB.
.SH MUTATIONS
Every mutation sends a cryptographically random 128\-bit idempotency key unless
.BI \-\-idempotency\-key " value"
is supplied. The CLI sends one request and never retries a mutation. Mutations
that support optimistic concurrency expose
.BI \-\-expected\-revision " value" .
.PP
Repeating a committed key with the same canonical request returns the recorded
result. Reusing it for another request returns
.BR idempotency.conflict .
.B mutation.indeterminate
means the server crashed during an external effect and will not repeat that key
automatically.
.PP
.B workspace run
and
.B pane run
preserve exact argument arrays after
.BR \-\- .
The client never reads or expands
.BR $SHELL .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success or clean stream completion.
.TP
.B 1
Structured server error.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid CLI syntax or local parameter validation failure.
.TP
.B 3
Connection, framing, timeout, or protocol failure.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CMUX_TUI_TERM
Override the terminal runtime default for child PTYs.
.B CMUX_MUX_TERM
is retained as a legacy fallback.
.TP
.B CMUX_MUX_CDP_URL
Attach browser panes to an existing Chrome DevTools Protocol endpoint instead
of launching a browser. Both
.B ws://
and
.B http://
endpoints are supported;
.B wss://
is not.
.TP
.B TMPDIR
Base directory for the default session socket path.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $TMPDIR/cmux\-tui\-<uid>/<session>.sock
Default session socket.
.TP
.I cmux\-tui.json
Session configuration, including
.B machine_sidebar
and
.B machines
entries for the machine rail, and
.B browser
settings for browser panes.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Start the default session:
.PP
.RS
.B cmux
.RE
.PP
Start a named session without attaching:
.PP
.RS
.B cmux \-\-headless \-\-session agents
.RE
.PP
Create a workspace and run a command in it:
.PP
.RS
.B cmux workspace create \-\-name api
.br
.B cmux workspace current run \-\- cargo test
.RE
.PP
Follow session events as JSON lines:
.PP
.RS
.B cmux session current events \-\-jsonl
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cmux\-relay (1),
.BR tmux (1)
.PP
Full documentation is in the
.B cmux\-tui/docs
directory of the source distribution, and at
.IR https://github.com/sweetcornna/cmux-for-linux .
.SH LICENSE
GPL\-3.0\-or\-later. See
.I /usr/share/licenses/cmux/LICENSE
for the complete text and
.I /usr/share/doc/cmux/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md
for third\-party notices.
